  "title": "Hamming Ball Covering Growth",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r$ be fixed and let $H(r)$ be the Hamming ball of radius $r$ in $\\mathbb{F}_2^n$. Let $f(r)$ be the smallest constant such that there exist infinitely many $n$ with subspaces $V_n \\leq \\mathbb{F}_2^n$ satisfying $V_n + H(r) = \\mathbb{F}_2^n$ and $|V_n| = (f(r) + o(1)) \\frac{2^n}{|H(r)|}$. Does $f(r) \\to \\infty$?",
    "sha256": "8ea3d6f4468cec173bb3136b7c220396c41ccd4c129d43c4579133568c0c854a",
